For every stack $\mathbf{W} = (W_c)_{c \in C}$:


(a) $\operatorname{gp}(\mathbf{W}) \le g^{-\operatorname{rank} \mathbf{W}}$, with equality if the row space of $\mathbf{W}$ is spanned by unit vectors $e_i$ with $i \in [N]$;
(b) $\operatorname{gp}(v^\top) \ge \operatorname{gp}(\mathbf{W})$ for every $v$ in the row space of $\mathbf{W}$.

For an admissible choice of evaluation points and a symmetric matrix $W \in \mathbb{F}_q^{(N+1) \times (N+1)}$, the following are equivalent:


(a) $W$ passes the tests of $S$ (Definition 4.2);
(b) $P_W(X) - W_{00}\, L_\rho(X) = h(X)\, Z(X)\, (X - \rho) + Z_0(X)\, R(X)$ for a polynomial $h(X)$ and an allowed polynomial $R(X)$;
(c) $P_W(X) = h'(X)\, Z(X) + Z_0(X)\, R(X)$ for a polynomial $h'(X)$ and an allowed polynomial $R(X)$.

In (b) and (c), $R(X)$ is the polynomial $R_W(X) \in \mathbb{F}_q^{<\nu n_{\mathsf{c}}}[X]$ with $R_W(p) = P_W(p)/Z_0(p)$ for every $p$ in the cosets, $h(X) \in \mathbb{F}_q^{<D-1}[X]$, and $h'(X) \in \mathbb{F}_q^{<D}[X]$.

Under the hypotheses of Theorem 5.9, if $\mathcal{A}$ runs in time $t$ and makes at most $Q_H$ queries to each of $H_{\mathsf{seed}}$ and $H_{\mathsf{key}}$, then $\mathcal{B}_0$ and $\mathcal{B}_1$ run in time at most
\begin{equation}
 t + 148\, Q + (d_R + 5)\, Q_H + C_R + 2 T_{\mathsf{LIFT}} , \quad C_R := 8 I + 3 L + 2 C_{\mathrm{post}} + C_{\mathrm{set}} + C_{\mathrm{desc}} ,
\end{equation}
where $I$, $C_{\mathrm{post}}$, $C_{\mathrm{set}}$, and $C_{\mathrm{desc}}$, sums given in the proof, and hence $C_R$, do not depend on $\mathcal{A}$, and $T_{\mathsf{LIFT}}$, the time of the lifting step, is polynomial in $N$ and $\log q$ (Lemma B.9, by (P3) and (P4)). We call this bound $t_R$; it is $t + O(Q + d_R\, Q_H + \mu) + \mathsf{poly}(D, \log q)$, as $C_R = O((N + n) D + \mu)$, $N < D$, and $n \le D$.
